# DBUG1 (stream S2-bodies, worker W12, EQ fuzz row 0x00dbf1a0) - a by-value struct result declared where the definition
# takes the result pointer explicitly (docs/PATCHES.md "DBUG1").

@@ DBUG1 src/havok/common/serialize/tagfile/binary/hkbinarytagfilewriter.cpp 0x00dbf1a0
# x86 0x00dbf1a0 (thiscall, `ret 4`): `lea eax,[esp+0x24]; push eax; mov ecx,ebx; call 0x00dba6a0` (an uninitialised
# stack temporary as the single stack word, ecx = the handle), then `push eax; mov ecx,edi; call 0x00dbf1a0` (the
# returned pointer is the argument of the recursive call) and `lea ecx,[esp+0x24]; call 0x00dba660` (the destructor on
# the temporary). The callee 0x00dba6a0 (hkdataobject.cpp, `void* FUN_00dba6a0_cls::SetShiftedValue(void* pTarget)`,
# `ret 4`) calls its owner's virtual slot 4 (vtable +0x10), hands
# the result to 0x00dba650 on pTarget (ecx) and returns pTarget in eax: an MSVC hidden result pointer, written out as
# an explicit parameter. MSVC lowers `S_dbf1a0_Handle f() const` and `void* f(void* out)` to the same code, GCC
# does not (the by-value struct comes back through the indirect-result register x8, the definition reads x1), so the
# native callee wrote through an undefined pointer. Fix: declare the member with the explicit out-pointer the
# definition has and pass a temporary of the same type that lives to the end of the full expression (its destructor
# FUN_00dba660 runs there, as the by-value result's did). MSVC keeps the original text (byte-identical by
# construction). The reference's decoration changes (units_renames.tsv).
<<<
    S_dbf1a0_Handle __thiscall SetShiftedValue() const
===
#ifdef _MSC_VER
    S_dbf1a0_Handle __thiscall SetShiftedValue() const
#else
    void* __thiscall SetShiftedValue(void* apOut) const
#endif
    /* exception specification follows */
>>>
<<<
    int parentId = WriteHandle(ahHandle.SetShiftedValue());
===
#ifdef _MSC_VER
    int parentId = WriteHandle(ahHandle.SetShiftedValue());
#else
    int parentId = WriteHandle(*reinterpret_cast<S_dbf1a0_Handle*>(ahHandle.SetShiftedValue(
        const_cast<S_dbf1a0_Handle*>(&static_cast<const S_dbf1a0_Handle&>(S_dbf1a0_Handle())))));
#endif
>>>
